{
  "$comment": [
    "Built-in training program templates. See docs/adr/0007 for the terminology and the",
    "rotation-not-calendar decision.",
    "",
    "A SPLIT is how the body's musculature is divided across sessions -- full body, upper/lower,",
    "push-pull-legs. A PROGRAM is the split plus exercise selection and a set prescription, which",
    "is what these are. Progression is not in here: that is ProgressionEngine's job, session to",
    "session, and baking target loads into a template would freeze them.",
    "",
    "ORDERED, NOT SCHEDULED. No day-of-week appears anywhere, deliberately. 'Next in the rotation'",
    "survives a missed Monday; 'it's Wednesday, do legs' starts nagging the first time life",
    "happens.",
    "",
    "Set counts are per session. The weekly total per muscle is what actually matters (docs/adr",
    "/0010), and the app computes that from the rotation rather than asking anyone to do the",
    "arithmetic -- which is also how you can see, before committing, that a program leaves your",
    "biceps under the effective dose.",
    "",
    "Every exerciseId must exist in exercises.json; a test enforces it. Sessions deliberately lead",
    "with the biggest compound movements, because those are the ones worth doing while fresh.",
    "",
    "These are starting points, not prescriptions. The trainee can edit any of them."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "templates": [
